                ['q' => 'Is surgery the only treatment for appendicitis?', 'a' => 'In most cases, yes. Removing the inflamed appendix (appendicectomy) prevents it from bursting, which can cause a serious infection. Your surgeon will confirm the right plan after examination and tests.'],
                ['q' => 'How long does recovery take after appendix surgery?', 'a' => 'After laparoscopic surgery most patients go home within 1 to 2 days and return to light activity in about a week. Open surgery, or a ruptured appendix, may need a longer stay and recovery. Your surgeon will guide you on your own timeline.'],
