                ['q' => 'Do all gallstones need to be removed?', 'a' => 'Not always. Stones that cause no symptoms are often only watched. Surgery is usually advised once stones cause pain, infection or other complications.'],
                ['q' => 'Can I live normally without a gallbladder?', 'a' => 'Yes. The liver keeps making bile that flows directly into the intestine, so most people digest food normally after the gallbladder is removed. Start with light, low-fat meals and slowly return to your usual diet.'],
