            'items' => [
                ['q' => 'Will a hernia go away on its own?', 'a' => 'No. A hernia is a gap in the muscle wall and does not heal by itself. It usually grows over time, so surgical repair is the only permanent treatment.'],
                ['q' => 'What is the difference between open and laparoscopic hernia repair?', 'a' => 'Laparoscopic repair uses a few tiny incisions and a camera and usually means less pain and quicker recovery. Open repair uses one incision over the hernia. Both commonly use a mesh, and your surgeon will suggest what suits you best.'],
                ['q' => 'When should a hernia be treated as an emergency?', 'a' => 'If the bulge becomes hard, tender or discoloured, or you have severe pain with vomiting or constipation, go to a surgeon immediately, as the hernia may be trapped.'],
