            'items' => [
                ['q' => 'Is a hydrocele dangerous, and does it need treatment?', 'a' => 'A hydrocele is usually harmless and painless, but scrotal swelling can also be caused by a hernia, infection or tumour, so it should be examined and confirmed with an ultrasound. Treatment is advised if it is large, uncomfortable or affects daily activities.'],
                ['q' => 'What is the treatment for a hydrocele?', 'a' => 'The standard treatment is a short operation called hydrocelectomy, which removes or closes the fluid sac. Needle aspiration with an injection is an option for some patients, though the fluid is more likely to return.'],
            ],
